Don't just read from your slides.

793
00:38:36,140 --> 00:38:37,220
Exactly.

794
00:38:37,220 --> 00:38:40,300
Slides are support, not your script.

795
00:38:40,300 --> 00:38:42,740
Now let's talk about common mistakes.

796
00:38:42,740 --> 00:38:45,920
Mistake number one, reading everything.

797
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:48,320
That makes your presentation boring.

798
00:38:48,320 --> 00:38:50,620
Speak naturally instead.

799
00:38:50,620 --> 00:38:53,780
Mistake number two, too much information.

800
00:38:53,780 --> 00:38:56,060
Keep it simple and focused.

801
00:38:56,060 --> 00:38:59,140
Mistake number three, no structure.

802
00:38:59,140 --> 00:39:02,300
Always organize your ideas clearly.

803
00:39:02,300 --> 00:39:05,580
Mistake number four, speaking too fast.

804
00:39:05,580 --> 00:39:07,820
Slow down and breathe.

805
00:39:07,820 --> 00:39:11,100
Mistake number five, lack of confidence.

806
00:39:11,100 --> 00:39:13,180
Practice is the solution.

807
00:39:13,180 --> 00:39:14,940
Now let's do a role play.

808
00:39:14,940 --> 00:39:15,900
Okay.

809
00:39:15,900 --> 00:39:18,300
Good morning, I talk about sales.

810
00:39:18,300 --> 00:39:20,900
Sales are important, thank you.

811
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:23,580
That's too short and unclear.

812
00:39:23,580 --> 00:39:25,080
Yes, I agree.

813
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:26,620
Let's improve it.

814
00:39:26,620 --> 00:39:27,500
Okay.

815
00:39:27,500 --> 00:39:30,520
Good morning everyone, thank you for being here.

816
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:33,960
Today, I'm going to talk about our sales performance.

817
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:36,920
First, I'll review last month's results,

818
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:40,120
then I'll discuss our strategy for improvement.

819
00:39:40,120 --> 00:39:43,440
Finally, I'll share our goals for next quarter.

820
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:45,160
Thank you for your attention.

821
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:48,080
That's perfect, structured and professional.

822
00:39:48,080 --> 00:39:50,880
Yes, it's structured and professional.

823
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:53,200
Now let's do a longer example.

824
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,160
Okay.

825
00:39:54,160 --> 00:39:55,600
Good afternoon, everyone.

826
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:56,840
My name is Daniel,

827
00:39:56,840 --> 00:39:59,760
and today I'll be presenting our marketing strategy.

828
00:39:59,760 --> 00:40:02,400
First, let's look at our current performance.

829
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:05,400
Over the past three months, we have seen steady growth.

830
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:09,520
For example, our online sales increased by 15%.

831
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:11,720
Now let's move on to our strategy.

832
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:14,120
We plan to focus more on social media

833
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:15,760
and digital advertising.

834
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:19,680
Finally, our goal is to increase revenue by 25%

835
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:20,920
in the next quarter.

836
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,600
Thank you for your attention.

837
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:26,520
That's excellent, clear, structured, and professional.

838
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:27,400
Thank you.

839
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:30,480
Now let's talk about handling questions.

840
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:33,720
Yes, this is very important in presentations.

841
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:37,400
After your presentation, people may ask questions.

842
00:40:37,400 --> 00:40:39,840
And you need to respond professionally.

843
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:42,520
You can say, that's a great question.

844
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:44,760
Or, thank you for your question.

845
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:47,440
If you don't understand, you can say,

846
00:40:47,440 --> 00:40:49,880
could you please repeat the question?

847
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:52,520
Or, could you clarify your question?

848
00:40:52,520 --> 00:40:54,600
If you don't know the answer.

849
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:58,100
You can say, I'll need to check that and get back to you.

850
00:40:58,100 --> 00:41:00,540
That's honest and professional.

851
00:41:00,540 --> 00:41:02,860
Now let's do a Q&A role play.

852
00:41:02,860 --> 00:41:03,780
Okay.

853
00:41:03,780 --> 00:41:06,700
What are the main challenges in your strategy?

854
00:41:06,700 --> 00:41:08,340
That's a great question.

855
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:11,220
One of the main challenges is competition.

856
00:41:11,220 --> 00:41:14,940
However, we're working on improving our unique value.

857
00:41:14,940 --> 00:41:16,380
Very good answer.

858
00:41:16,380 --> 00:41:17,340
Thank you.

859
00:41:17,340 --> 00:41:19,580
Now let's talk about confidence.

860
00:41:19,580 --> 00:41:22,580
Confidence is key in presentations.

861
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:24,700
Even if your English is not perfect,

862
00:41:24,700 --> 00:41:27,100
confidence makes a big difference.

863
00:41:27,100 --> 00:41:31,700
Yes, speak clearly, smile, and believe in yourself.

864
00:41:31,700 --> 00:41:34,700
Practice is the best way to build confidence.

865
00:41:34,700 --> 00:41:36,860
Practice in front of a mirror.

866
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:38,620
Or record yourself.

867
00:41:38,620 --> 00:41:40,660
Or practice with a friend.

868
00:41:40,660 --> 00:41:43,460
The more you practice, the better you become.

869
00:41:43,460 --> 00:41:44,960
Absolutely.

870
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,660
Now let's wrap up.

871
00:41:46,660 --> 00:41:50,020
Today, we learned how to improve presentation skills

872
00:41:50,020 --> 00:41:51,500
in business English.

873
00:41:51,500 --> 00:41:56,460
We covered structure, useful phrases, delivery, and common mistakes.

874
00:41:56,460 --> 00:42:00,140
We also practiced real examples and role plays.

875
00:42:00,140 --> 00:42:04,460
The most important thing is to be clear, simple, and confident.

876
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:05,780
Exactly.

877
00:42:05,780 --> 00:42:07,940
Keep practicing every day.

878
00:42:07,940 --> 00:42:10,180
And don't be afraid to speak.

879
00:42:10,180 --> 00:42:12,140
Thank you so much for listening.

880
00:42:12,140 --> 00:42:14,860
Keep learning and improving your English.

881
00:42:14,860 --> 00:42:16,820
We'll see you in the next episode.

882
00:42:16,820 --> 00:42:18,220
Goodbye, everyone.

883
00:42:18,220 --> 00:42:19,220
Goodbye.
